  "description": {
    "sub_id3": null,
    "sub_name": "水文學",
    "sub_ename": "HYDROLOGY",
    "describe_ch": "水為人類生存的三要素之一，而水的利用、保護及災害防治，是為水利工程師的職志，認識水的形成、分佈、運移則為水利工程師的基本素養。本課程將介紹水在陸地生成及運移循環過程中之數個水文現象，包括降雨、截留、窪蓄、蒸發、入滲、地下水等單元。\r\n",
    "describe_eh": "Taiwan has the highest rate of precipitation of any developed country in the world, but it is known as a “water-starved island.” Global warming, climate change, and sea-level rise are environmental threats; and, sponge cities, living with floods, and rooms for the rivers are the new trends for solving above. These above can be understood by hydrology. This course will start from hydrological recycle, then introduce the fundamental topics inside, including rainfall, evaporation/ evapotranspiration, depression, infiltration and ground water.",
    "pre_subname": "",
    "pre_sub_id3": null,
    "pre_sub_ename": "",
    "pre_describe": null,
    "pre_describe_en": null,
    "scr_credit": 3.0
  },
  "targets": [
    {
      "seq": 1,
      "describe_ch": "瞭解水文學的定義及重要性\t",
      "describe_en": "1 Understand the definition and importance of hydrology."
    },
    {
      "seq": 2,
      "describe_ch": "認識基本水文循環各單元的現象及物理機制\n\t",
      "describe_en": "2 Learn the hydrologic cycle and its mechanism.\n"
    },
    {
      "seq": 3,
      "describe_ch": "理解與應用水文循環各單元之量化分析法\n\t",
      "describe_en": "3 Learn how to quantify the existence, distribution, movement and phenomena of water in hydrologic cycle.\n"
    }
  ],
